<content>
  <section><title>Writing Quadratics in Different Forms</title>
<note>
  <para><emphasis>Three Common Quadratic Forms:</emphasis></para>
  <para>The vertex form of a quadratic function is \(f(x)=a(x-h)^2+k\) where \((h, k)\) is the vertex.</para>
  <para>The factored form of the quadratic function is \(f(x)=(x-a)(x-b)\) where \(a\) and \(b\) are roots of \(f(x)\).</para>
</note>
<para>For questions 1 - 2, use the function \(f(x)=(x-2)(x+8)\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Write the function in standard form. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - </emphasis>multiply the binomials using distribution (FOIL).</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 - </emphasis>Simplify.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> Write the function from question 1 in vertex form. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 - </emphasis>Complete the square.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Balance the equation. </para>
<para>Finally, factor the trinomial and simplify.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Rewrite the function in standard form: \(f(x)=6(x−2)^2+4\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> -Expand the square.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 - </emphasis>Distribute the constant.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Simplify like terms</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>Rewrite the function in standard form: \(f(x)=5(x−3)^2+2\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Expand the square.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Distribute the constant.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Simplify like terms</para>
<title>Try It: Writing Quadratic Functions in Equivalent Forms</title>
<!--Q#-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Write the function \(f(x)=(x+5)(x+3)\) in vertex form.</para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>
      First, multiply the binomials using distribution (FOIL).</para>
    <para>Then, simplify.</para>
    <para>Now, write this function in vertex form.</para>
    <para>Balance the equation. Add the constant to the quadratic to complete the square and subtract it from the original constant.</para>
    <para>Finally, factor the trinomial and simplify.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
</content>
